.\" Originally written by Jan Schaumann
.\" <jschauma@netmeister.org> in October 2026.
.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt emudhra-cleanup 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm emudhra-cleanup
.Nd prune CA bundles from eMudhra related root certificates
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Vbhlv
.Op Fl d Ar path
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Op Fl p Ar pip
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
command attempts to remove eMudhra related root
certificates from common CA bundles.
.Sh OPTIONS
The following options are supported by
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -width __file__
.It Fl V
Print version number and exit.
.It Fl b
Create a backup file of any modified bundles.
.It Fl d Ar path
Try to detect CA bundles containing the roots located
under
.Ar path ,
but don't modify them.
Can be specified multiple times.
.It Fl f Ar file
Prune this given file or directory.
Can be specified multiple times.
.It Fl h
Print a short usage statement and exit.
.It Fl l
Enable diagnostic logging.
.It Fl p Ar path
Fix the given pip.
.Ar path
must be an absolute path to a pip or python
executable.
.It Fl v
Be verbose.
Can be specified multiple times to increase verbosity.
.El
.Sh DETAILS
Many of the code examples shown online to update CA
bundles to remove the root CA certificates affected by
the eMudhra compromise assume that a cert bundle
contains comments annotating the certificates, but
that is not always the case.
If you have bundles that consist entirely and only of
PEM certificates, those commands will not remove the
affected roots.
.Pp
Instead, you'd have to decode each certificate or
compare the entire PEM blob.
That's tedious.
.Pp
.Nm
is intended to help complete this task.
It will look for the roots in a few common places, or
let you specify a bundle using the
.Fl f
flag.
.Pp
If the
.Fl d
flag is specified,
.Nm
will either inspect the given bundle, or search the
given path for likely candidates and output those that
contain the roots in question.
.Pp
Note: the search is done using
.Xr find 1
with the
.Xr x
flag, meaning you have to specify each mount point
explicitly.
.Sh LOGGING
If the
.Fl l
flag is specified,
.Nm
will log diagnostic messages using
.Xr logger 1
with a tag of 'emudhra-cleanup'.
.Sh CA BUNDLES
By default,
.Nm
will look in a few common locations for files that are
likely to be CA cert bundles.
Specifically, it looks at the following:
.Bl
.It
/etc/ssl/cert.pem
.It
/etc/ssl/ca-bundle.pem
.It
/etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt
.It
/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt
.El
.Pp
If the directory '/opt/homebrew' exists, then
.Nm
will also consider the files
\'/opt/homebrew/etc/*/cert.pem'.
.Pp
If the file '/etc/ca-certificates.conf' exists,
.Nm
will add exclusion parameters to it and subsequently
attempt to run
.Xr update-ca-certificates 8 .
.Pp
If the
.Fl f
flag is given, only the specified
.Ar file(s)
will be considered.
.Sh ROOTS REMOVED
.Nm
removes the following root CA certificates from the CA
bundles it operates on:
.Bl
.It
emSign Root TLS CA - G3
7DD78D5F4F13459A83DFF9ABBBA62EDBAF6F2D102BF257FD712F4D9F2746ED8D
.It
emSign Root CS CA - G3
F2EDAAFF3D9B701FB4D14C9F285F8C0BAD90FC3BCC1FA07D47F4718EDABA34A5
.It
emSign ECC Root CA - G3
86A1ECBA089C4A8D3BBE2734C612BA341D813E043CF9E8A862CD5C57A36BBE6B
.It
AAA Certificate Services
D7A7A0FB5D7E2731D771E9484EBCDEF71D5F0C3E0A2948782BC83EE0EA699EF4
.El
.Sh PIP
Python's "pip" may use a built-in CA bundle.
.Nm
can try to point pip to a fixed CA bundle.
For this, specify the python or pip executable via the
.Fl p
flag.
.Nm
will update (or create, if it does not yet exist) the
\'sitecustomize.py' configuration file to set the
.Ev PIP_CERT
environment variable.
.Pp
If the current process's environment does not have
this variable set, then
.Nm
will set the value in 'sitecustomize.py' to the file
.Ar /etc/ssl/cert.pem ,
if it exists.
.Sh EXAMPLES
To verbosely fix the default set of CA bundles, while
logging all messages and creating backup files of each
modified bundle:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
emudhra-cleanup -b -l -v -v -v -v
.Ed
.Pp
To check, but not modify, all CA bundles under /usr/local:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
emudhra-cleanup -d /usr/local
.Ed
.Pp
To check, but not modify, specific files:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
emudhra-cleanup -d /usr/local/etc/cert.pem -d /etc/mycerts.pem
.Ed
.Pp
To update homebrew's pip3.11:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
emudhra-cleanup -p /opt/homebrew/bin/pip3.11
.Ed
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width PIP_CERT
.It Ev PIP_CERT
The path name to the bundle to use for python/pip.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
was originally written by
.An Jan Schaumann
.Aq jschauma@netmeister.org
in October 2026.
